Article 2 (Scope)
The term "judges of the rank of presiding judge of a high court or higher" in statutes, etc. means judges appointed to any of the following positions: Provided, That the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court and the Justices of the Supreme Court shall be excluded where statutes, etc. separately provide for them. <Amended on February 18, 2013; December 31, 2013; February 19, 2016; February 2, 2017; January 8, 2018; February 1, 2019; January 29, 2021; and March 25, 2021.>
1. Chief Justice of the Supreme Court;
2. Justice of the Supreme Court;
3. President of the Judicial Research and Training Institute or President of the Judicial Policy Research Institute;
4. President of a court at any level;
5. Vice Minister of the National Court Administration;
6. Chief Judicial Research Officer or Senior Judicial Research Officer of the Supreme Court;
7. Director of the Court Library;
8. Chief of Staff to the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court;
9. Head of an office of the National Court Administration;
10. Chief Professor of the Judicial Research and Training Institute, Chief Research Fellow of the Judicial Policy Research Institute, or Standing Member of the Sentencing Commission;
11. Presiding judge of a high court or the Patent Court;
12. Deleted on January 29, 2021;
13. Deleted on February 19, 2016;
14. A judge appointed as a professor at the Judicial Research and Training Institute after having served in a position specified in subparagraphs 3 through 11;
15. A judge who formerly held a position specified in subparagraphs 3 through 11 or 14 and for whom three years have not elapsed since being appointed to a position other than those positions.
